# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/
node_modules/
dashboard/**/node_modules/
dashboard/**/dist/
dashboard/shared/*.js

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
office.config.local.yaml
profiles/*.local.yaml
.socraticode.local.yaml
.worktrees/
.superpowers/

# Knowledge Librarian runtime audits (local, non-TASK artifacts)
knowledge-reviews/


# runs/ — team-synced task state (allowlist; logs and generated files stay local)
runs/*
!runs/*/
runs/*/*
!runs/*/task.md
!runs/*/status.yaml
!runs/*/*-output.yaml
!runs/*/decision.yaml
# Staleness marks are a CONSTRAINT on what a capture may claim, so they must be
# team-synced and their deletion must be visible in git. Left ignored, dropping
# the ledger silently turned a blocked `current` claim into a passing one and
# `git status` showed nothing.
!runs/*/evidence-freshness.yaml
# Same argument for preflight decisions: the record is what says an externally-
# sourced dispatch was gated and on what grounds. Ignored, deleting it would be
# invisible in `git status` AND would silently reset the pf-NNN counter, so a
# denial could be erased and overwritten by a later allow under the same id.
!runs/*/preflight.yaml
!runs/*/verification-evidence.md
!runs/*/findings.md
!runs/*/win-definition-spec.md
!runs/.gitkeep

runs/*/*.log
runs/*/.cursor-prompt.md
runs/*/meta.yaml
runs/*/status.yaml.corrupt.*

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
